 "subtitle": "The plain DreamerV3 runs on main: 1.1M env steps each, size50m, scored on the same 30 fixed worlds with tools/death_eval.py. Family runs are indexed in README.md and documented on their branches. Updated 2026-11-08.",
 "summary": "Every number is the mean episode-final achievement count over 30 evaluation episodes, ± its standard error over those worlds; unlock rates are the share of episodes in which an achievement fired; return is the mean raw Craftax return as a % of the maximum (226). Every checkpoint is scored on the same fixed worlds (env.reseed, audit B05), so comparisons are paired world by world. The error bars cover the worlds only, not training seeds.\nPlain DreamerV3 on the fixed code (abl_plain, seed 0) scores 4.77 ± 0.28, level with vanilla DreamerV3 on the original code (4.63 ± 0.22). Normalized return: 1.71% and 1.65%.",
 "table_note": "ach. ± SE = mean episode-final achievements ± standard error over the 30 worlds. w/o wake = the same minus WAKE_UP. life = mean lifespan in steps. return = raw Craftax return, % of 226. Rates are % of episodes. Vanilla DreamerV3: the original checkpoint (code before the 2026-10 fixes), re-scored on the fixed worlds. Plain (new code): this branch's code, `--configs craftax size50m --env.craftax.survival none`; the row shows seed 0.",
